QEMU, AND OUR CHANGE TO IT

launcher/qemu-windows/keephaven-qemu.nix is NOT in that list and is GPL-2.0-only.
It is the script that controls the compilation of the QEMU binary we redistribute,
which GPL-2.0 section 3 counts as part of that binary's corresponding source, so it
cannot be withheld whoever wrote it. It travels on every drive as
qemu-build-recipe.nix, with flake.lock beside it as qemu-build-flake.lock.

launcher/qemu-windows/win32-hdev-fixed-length.patch is a change to QEMU's own
block/file-win32.c. It is a derivative of GPL-2.0 code and is therefore
GPL-2.0 whoever wrote it. It cannot be licensed under LICENSE.txt and it is not
offered under other terms. The QEMU binary built from it is GPL-2.0 as well.
Every drive carries QEMU's licence, that patch in full, and a written offer
of the complete corresponding source, good for three years.

